{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/773737-solitary-confinement-used-for-blind-gun-gadget","id":773737,"title":"Solitary Confinement used for Blind Gun gadget","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-25T01:35:59-08:00","id":773737,"title":"Solitary Confinement used for Blind Gun gadget","content":"I want to build a gadget, using Solitary Confinement which would blind the person being shot at. (Well it doesn't really have to be a gun). <br /> <br /> What I really want, is a gadget to blind a demon, using Solitary Confinement. How would one build such a device? How would it be defended against? <br /> <br /> At the moment, I imagine an alien looking gun, shooting big bolts of darkness out of the rip of reality, which is Solitary Confinement, and upon hit it blinds the target. But I'm not sure on emchanics, and how to defend against the gun (given, that the gun will be used against a PC, such things cannot be handwaved)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T04:32:06-08:00","id":773818,"title":"","content":"I would say that It should inflict the blinded tilt as a temporary affect for 1-3 turns, maybe 1 per success but something short like that, removing sight is a big deal. I'd almost say a near field effect of deafen would be a simpler base to work with ( Blind temporally instead of deafen) but thematically it could still work with solitary confinement.<br /> <br /> For the activation roll I would say it should either be a Dexterity + Firearms - Stamina or a contested roll of Dexterity + Firearms Vs Stamina + Supernatural tolerance<br /> <br /> For the hardware I do agree that a gun firing 'globs' of darkness that cling to someone's face / eyes would work to explain the effect.<br /> <br /> For how someone could defend against that attack (if you feel a mere penalty or contested roll isn't enough) potentially it could require direct line of sight to the target's eyes or some such restriction. This way shielding your eyes (willing but controlled blindness) or even mirrored sunglasses could potentially be enough to defend against it. I personally would prefer a better flaw than what I gave as examples but I honestly am drawing a blank.<br /> <br /> I also suggest to make sure that even if it has a fatal flaw (like being defeated by sunglasses) do try to make sure that your PCs don't feel like they cannot do anything while affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}